/*!
    \page sonicinitinfo-index.html
    \title Sonic Init Info

    Sonic Init Info tells SonicDE components, at runtime, which init system and
    seat manager the machine is running. Code can then do the right thing on
    systemd, OpenRC, runit, s6, dinit, sysvinit and the BSDs instead of
    assuming systemd.

    \list
    \li \l Sonic::InitInfo: what runs as PID 1, what manages services and
        seats, whether journald runs, and the VT a display manager starts on.
    \endlist

    None of this needs root. Nothing is cached; callers keep the result.

    \code
    using namespace Sonic::InitInfo;

    if (serviceManager() == ServiceManager::OpenRC) {
        // use rc-service / rc-update
    }
    \endcode

    \section1 Using the Module

    \section2 Building with CMake

    Use the \c find_package() command to locate the SonicInitInfo package and
    link against its target:

    \badcode
    find_package(SonicInitInfo REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE Sonic::InitInfo)
    \endcode

    \section1 API Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Sonic Init Info C++ Classes}
    \endlist
*/
